<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Persians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Persians are an Iranian people whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> lay in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pars">Pars</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. They founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, and Persian culture and administration shaped successor states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>. Persian bureaucrats, scholars and artists served many empires across western and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p></div>
